WHY THIS WORKS
- asks for the email first and does nothing else until it arrives
- sends the masterclass only after the address is in hand
- three short messages, not one block of instructions

CONVERSATION 1: straightforward

Lead: Booked! Tuesday at 2.

Sonia: Great, Tuesday's in.

Which email did you use to book?

Lead: r.castillo@example.com

Sonia: Got it, thank you.

I've sent my masterclass to that address. Worth watching before Tuesday so the call can start further along.

{{masterclass_link}}

Natalia will text you beforehand. Reply to her so your slot stays confirmed.

Lead: Perfect, will do.

Sonia: See you on the other side of Tuesday.

CONVERSATION 2: she says thanks first and sends the email later

Lead: ok thanks!

Sonia: Before you go, which email did you use to book? I'll send you something worth watching first.

Lead: sorry, missed this. it's jen.okafor@example.com

Sonia: No problem at all.

